    "rationale": "The 1-block floor is 1.81 us/launch and a graph is 1.11x vs a native loop. BUT this 1-block floor is only the launch-submission part; the --grid-sweep shows per-launch cost SCALES with grid size (GPU workgroup scheduling): real hot kernels launch thousands of blocks, so their ~20 us/op dispatch residual is command-processor-bound, NOT host/Python (M14.dispatch.1 removed Python and was parity) and NOT arg-marshaling. A native verify loop (M16.2) calls the same hipLaunchKernelGGL with the same grids -> it cannot reduce this -> predicted PARITY. Graphs (M16.5) are also ~neutral even at large grids. The only lever is FEWER launches and MORE compute-per-launch (M16.3 megakernels) so dispatch is paid fewer times and hidden behind compute, plus lower kernel time (M16.4).",
